{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-028",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 28,
  "title": "Proverbs 28",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 28",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 28,
  "sortOrder": 20028,
  "verseCount": 28,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For the transgression of a land many are the princes thereof: but by a man of understanding and knowledge the state thereof shall be prolonged.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "A poor man that oppresseth the poor is like a sweeping rain which leaveth no food.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "They that forsake the law praise the wicked: but such as keep the law contend with them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Evil men understand not judgment: but they that seek the LORD understand all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Better is the poor that walketh in his uprightness, than he that is perverse in his ways, though he be rich.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Whoso keepeth the law is a wise son: but he that is a companion of riotous men shameth his father.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "He that by usury and unjust gain increaseth his substance, he shall gather it for him that will pity the poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He that turneth away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer shall be abomination.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Whoso causeth the righteous to go astray in an evil way, he shall fall himself into his own pit: but the upright shall have good things in possession.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The rich man is wise in his own conceit; but the poor that hath understanding searcheth him out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "When righteous men do rejoice, there is great glory: but when the wicked rise, a man is hidden.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Happy is the man that feareth alway: but he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "As a roaring lion, and a ranging bear; so is a wicked ruler over the poor people.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The prince that wanteth understanding is also a great oppressor: but he that hateth covetousness shall prolong his days.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "A man that doeth violence to the blood of any person shall flee to the pit; let no man stay him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Whoso walketh uprightly shall be saved: but he that is perverse in his ways shall fall at once.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain persons shall have poverty enough.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "A faithful man shall abound with blessings: but he that maketh haste to be rich shall not be innocent.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "To have respect of persons is not good: for for a piece of bread that man will transgress.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He that hasteth to be rich hath an evil eye, and considereth not that poverty shall come upon him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "He that rebuketh a man afterwards shall find more favour than he that flattereth with the tongue.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Whoso robbeth his father or his mother, and saith, It is no transgression; the same is the companion of a destroyer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "He that is of a proud heart stirreth up strife: but he that putteth his trust in the LORD shall be made fat.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack: but he that hideth his eyes shall have many a curse.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:28:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "When the wicked rise, men hide themselves: but when they perish, the righteous increase.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 28:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:28:28"
      }
    }
  ],
